#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114885 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/assets/9e23d542bfc56d506f5437a35a92c304d618109ef60086e1f5a7a4fee57d8a80.png) and $u(t) = t.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114886 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114887 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6272e646-6faf-5cbf-9aa8-bfa1c9a1a5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305617} {:answer/id #uuid "61492250-b27b-5c47-b317-b118914c4bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305618} {:answer/id #uuid "41c31433-12c8-5113-bb33-8079400d618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305619} {:answer/id #uuid "12a7c4c0-521d-5b22-8f03-585838f052b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305620} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621} :answer-field/id #uuid "41aec396-46ce-51ab-bf41-4cb56972babe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7bf0574-f62a-50b0-b258-2bfc1dfc7afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327246} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7bb0f9-8241-59dc-84ef-242b9967874d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327247} {:answer/id #uuid "81115a2c-3ebf-5dbb-8c65-2bfdae0f1bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327248} {:answer/id #uuid "307dc8bb-869b-5538-9834-e9edbffc46d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327249} {:answer/id #uuid "2426cc07-f1a0-516d-bfd0-c142e3b4a6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81115a2c-3ebf-5dbb-8c65-2bfdae0f1bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327248} :answer-field/id #uuid "17609dc3-c229-5ca9-8caa-b4da3800c4cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffb6e1fe-344f-5ac5-bc61-6cb251c0c574" :question/math-academy-id "q-128481" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eaf27fa-d187-56ba-bd53-e57a7edb968d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368404} {:answer/id #uuid "9caa6041-8821-500b-be2d-2ab527a1f8d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368405} {:answer/id #uuid "39681e33-dd2b-582d-a931-73990782c709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368406} {:answer/id #uuid "d27f21ab-0598-5d91-87e4-8efb0e3690a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368407} {:answer/id #uuid "606f4088-3971-5397-a02e-038f42cba5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eaf27fa-d187-56ba-bd53-e57a7edb968d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368404} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab299f45-da79-5086-9c55-f784f600f8a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4198ce1e-0ba3-5a53-b852-015688085880" :question/math-academy-id "q-128572" :question/problem "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2({e}^{t}) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b029f1f-9e4a-597b-ae77-3d81c480f110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 14t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113463} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3d915b-79a3-5034-a5de-c06db5adfc1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 6t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113464} {:answer/id #uuid "24835394-1f04-511b-a157-cfeb639fa83e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 11t^{2} + 12t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113465} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa8e90-8b39-5545-99b0-87f760920652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 7t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113466} {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f83259c-d6e0-5a5d-835f-1cdded5c1c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a209f44d-4003-53ab-9d12-642d62514eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32298" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "875b016f-e8c7-5871-b60a-8140d518ab7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24t^{3} - 2t - 6 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 42t + 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113475} {:answer/id #uuid "d3cb532f-811d-5a4d-a2ae-e7f634a389c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-42t - 20 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 24t^{3} + 2t + 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113476} {:answer/id #uuid "14263be6-a304-5e5d-b176-0b1171e81f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t + 20 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113477} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6e72a8-69da-5220-88ac-e36adeb439a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 42t + 20 \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113478} {:answer/id #uuid "686fc5d6-9d73-5924-be7e-292fc0f83dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21t + 10 \\\\ 45t^{2} \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14263be6-a304-5e5d-b176-0b1171e81f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t + 20 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113477} :answer-field/id #uuid "18574eab-4e64-5ca8-b34a-644e09dffb17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54437c76-a800-5517-9d6f-6a2f64f033aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-32353" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f\\times\\mathbf g)'(t)$, where $$\\mathbf f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3t^2\\\\t+4\\\\8\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2\\\\-2t^2\\\\5t\\end{bmatrix}.$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Keeping the factors in order, $$\\mathbf f\\times\\mathbf g=\\begin{bmatrix}5t(t+4)+16t^2\\\\8(t+2)-15t^3\\\\-6t^4-(t+4)(t+2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}21t^2+20t\\\\8t+16-15t^3\\\\-6t^4-t^2-6t-8\\end{bmatrix}.$$ Differentiate each component to obtain $$(\\mathbf f\\times\\mathbf g)'(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20\\\\8-45t^2\\\\-24t^3-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}.$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b63046-d0c8-5b17-a680-40625cee930b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305687} {:answer/id #uuid "ce329a3c-d6dc-516e-8f1d-f962832405f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305688} {:answer/id #uuid "059f6fed-d4b0-5135-99a2-3f4b6890742c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305689} {:answer/id #uuid "f210782f-76de-5c66-920d-d343470da810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305690} {:answer/id #uuid "5291c699-50fe-522f-a333-7bba287e5b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce329a3c-d6dc-516e-8f1d-f962832405f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305688} :answer-field/id #uuid "e243c6fc-094b-525d-978b-2c3f8f5a01d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24bb40b1-a7b7-5eea-a633-757e31425152" :question/math-academy-id "q-32860" :question/problem "If $g(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ 5 \\\\ {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$, then  $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,5\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u(t)} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u(t)\\end{aligned}]{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e6f936-424e-5183-99e0-988712a9e068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327308} {:answer/id #uuid "dd050266-1870-5f15-86d6-f057084932d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327309} {:answer/id #uuid "43282c4f-790d-5cd6-8f5c-5659619f19d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327310} {:answer/id #uuid "0316b704-1192-5729-b51c-e89f67f5927d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327311} {:answer/id #uuid "ce59a7ac-bc7f-5eba-9140-a5898f3e51be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43282c4f-790d-5cd6-8f5c-5659619f19d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327310} :answer-field/id #uuid "a97f65b0-6b8d-55ab-80d3-18a5b299a6ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17db3926-f364-5101-a69e-c1d34df6ed10" :question/math-academy-id "q-33122" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6ef7c57-c032-526f-aa67-9b807706273d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305701} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f1b81-3a1c-50da-a2e3-89884eb7b89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305702} {:answer/id #uuid "4df4329c-21d2-51a8-b053-05bb883f4820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305703} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6c3d1f-8052-5990-80a0-a5b0872c3f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305704} {:answer/id #uuid "76ca5026-3449-5cf6-9238-64cc4803d070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4df4329c-21d2-51a8-b053-05bb883f4820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305703} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0dcda6-9c3c-5e46-bfc9-36ecd5a93d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9342327c-ff4e-553a-a4f4-0263c91cce83" :question/math-academy-id "q-33260" :question/problem "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64a0a43f-3b9f-5f8c-9f84-12d03178410f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327322} {:answer/id #uuid "b67cd514-5d5b-5d26-a442-dc0a758efd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327323} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2a9f7c-05cf-55be-8894-f40cc879a7bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327324} {:answer/id #uuid "6916f06b-5480-5608-a66d-48411b7564d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327325} {:answer/id #uuid "d26b33c4-f4dd-5a63-8fd1-2e4e42c63241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d26b33c4-f4dd-5a63-8fd1-2e4e42c63241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf695ad-3e17-535e-b5ef-925f18c49390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ab16987-2b95-50b0-9362-48aafca307ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-33446" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}})=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05484b82-e643-5284-8e00-d4814d2288e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305708} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d5b0f9-2539-56b6-9648-0c55489f2f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305709} {:answer/id #uuid "470c60d0-d3cc-5b8c-a4e2-3b13f679e832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305710} {:answer/id #uuid "248144a4-5195-507c-8ead-000ee1a6fcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305711} {:answer/id #uuid "b3341c7a-9b22-5378-a166-37514edd7b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3341c7a-9b22-5378-a166-37514edd7b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305712} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f07d3e-2650-56d7-8ae3-434d0181b857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6942209a-90ad-5fb0-92e6-b66937204d70" :question/math-academy-id "q-70681" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7b55457-c9f9-5d0c-a7e9-237db15ce839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327329} {:answer/id #uuid "2f64baa6-ed0b-583d-a7b4-3b54733334ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327330} {:answer/id #uuid "23d3cbec-6609-5443-aa68-9e52f77ae151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327331} {:answer/id #uuid "03f1ed98-54a0-5162-a056-4a21bf99c171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ {e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327332} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2e139-02bf-500e-a4d6-71101d952c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2e139-02bf-500e-a4d6-71101d952c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327333} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccdcf9ec-f301-5cf0-88ef-a2e67a7aa2a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c43762c8-310f-5f86-a903-48bba629edc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70695" :question/problem "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {u}^{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 3{u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ 3(u(t))^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u(t)}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3({e}^{t})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aeeda8b-f3e7-50f2-a525-f9cb1e45a466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736} {:answer/id #uuid "c09beb1e-6b5c-56d7-b309-e875013fcead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305737} {:answer/id #uuid "832905e6-89d2-51f6-bbcf-7292d3c655a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+{t}^{3}){e}^{t} \\\\ 4t \\\\ {t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305738} {:answer/id #uuid "f83193ff-79e3-5957-8133-1271d5f93bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(1-{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 8t \\\\ (t+{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305739} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cf90ca-8fb4-531d-84f4-9a72ecd5ecd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09beb1e-6b5c-56d7-b309-e875013fcead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305737} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1767873-42c2-57e8-b756-71d928f53399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d3825fa-4a39-5efb-9247-5f4f19ce4d38" :question/math-academy-id "q-71230" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2t[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
